  "workflow_name": "DFT study of vacancy-induced magnetism",
  "definition": "A computational workflow using spin-polarized density functional theory (DFT) to investigate magnetism induced by point defects (primarily vacancies) in materials. The workflow involves constructing a supercell of the host material, introducing one or more defects, relaxing the atomic structure, performing spin-polarized electronic structure calculations, extracting magnetic moments and band topology, and analyzing the origin of magnetism via projected densities of states, spin density, and Bader charge analysis.",
